  "Question": "Calculate the value of \\((2+1)(2^2+1)(2^4+1)(2^8+1)\\).",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "65535",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "After multiplying by \\((2-1)=1\\), apply the difference of squares formula repeatedly to obtain \\(2^{16}-1=65535\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Evaluate the factors and multiply\n\nThe powers are small enough to evaluate each factor directly. The four factors are \\(3\\), \\(5\\), \\(17\\), and \\(257\\), so multiplying in order gives\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n3\\cdot5\\cdot17\\cdot257\n&=15\\cdot17\\cdot257\\\\\n&=255\\cdot257\\\\\n&=65535.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThus the value is \\(65535\\).",
